{"id": "Mercury_7132020", "question": "Which part of an atom has the least mass?", "step_idx": 0, "options": ["A): electron", "B): nucleus", "C): neutron", "D): proton"], "correct": "A", "initial_cot": "The question asks for the part of an atom with the least mass. To answer this, we need to consider the masses of the different parts of an atom.\nThe nucleus is made up of protons and neutrons. Protons and neutrons have a significant mass, so the nucleus is not the part with the least mass.\nElectrons have a very small mass compared to protons and neutrons. They are also much lighter than the nucleus.\nProtons and neutrons have a similar mass, but they are still much heavier than electrons.\nTherefore, the part of an atom with the least mass is the electron.\nThe best answer is A.<|eot_id|>", "initial_cot_probs": [1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0], "initial_probs": [0.539182186126709, 0.37057414650917053, 0.06439613550901413, 0.020906362682580948], "prediction": 0, "cot_prediction": 0, "cot_step": "The question asks for the part of an atom with the least mass.", "segmented_cot": ["The question asks for the part of an atom with the least mass.", "To answer this, we need to consider the masses of the different parts of an atom.", "The nucleus is made up of protons and neutrons.", "Protons and neutrons have a significant mass, so the nucleus is not the part with the least mass.", "Electrons have a very small mass compared to protons and neutrons.", "They are also much lighter than the nucleus.", "Protons and neutrons have a similar mass, but they are still much heavier than electrons.", "Therefore, the part of an atom with the least mass is the electron.", "The best answer is A.<|eot_id|>"], "unlearning_results": {"0": {"completion": "A): electron. Electrons have the least mass", "probs": [0.539182186126709, 0.37057414650917053, 0.06439613550901413, 0.020906362682580948], "prediction": 0, "target_cot_step": "The question asks for the part of an atom with the least mass.", "target_cot